course: dictionary
lesson: 9447
title: Words that get stuck
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how a voice behaves when it gets stuck. To stammer means to speak with pauses and repeated sounds, like «I-I-I don't know».
explain: A stammer is a speech condition. A person may repeat sounds, stretch them, or get stuck on words. Many people have a stammer, and it has nothing to do with how clever someone is.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Maya's friend Josh copied the way a boy talks with his stammer, and everyone laughed.» Copying and laughing show that this was unkind, not funny.
explain: When a classmate stammers, the kind thing is to wait patiently and not finish their words for them.
fact: Stammer can be a verb (he stammers, she stammered) or a noun (a stammer).
fact: «Stammer» means to speak with pauses and repeated sounds, or to get stuck on words.
fact: In the USA a stammer is often called a stutter.
fact: Speech therapists can help people who have a stammer.
fact: Having a stammer has nothing to do with how clever a person is.
exercise: «I-I-I don't know», said Ella, who began to stammer when the teacher looked at her. What does stammer mean? | To run away quickly | *To speak with pauses and repeated sounds | To sing very loudly | To write very neatly
exercise: When a classmate stammers, what is the kind thing to do? | Finish their words quickly so they can stop | Laugh so they feel better | Tell them to speak faster | *Wait patiently and do not finish their words
exercise: Which form of stammer is a noun, a thing you can have? | stammered | *a stammer | stammering | stammers
test: «Josh copied a boy's stammer and everyone laughed.» What does this sentence show? | The boy was being rude on purpose | Everyone was very impressed | *Laughing at a stammer was unkind | It was a funny story
test: A stammer is a speech condition. Which statement is true? | It only happens in stories | *It has nothing to do with how clever a person is | It means a person is less clever | It is the same thing as being rude
exam: Jayden asks, «Why should I not laugh when someone stammers?» What is the best answer? | *Because a stammer is a speech condition, and laughing hurts their feelings | Because stammers are always funny | Because it is a rule about lunch | Because you must finish their words for them
